A = \sum_{n=1}^{2}\frac{3^n}{\prod_{k=1}^{n} (k+3)} = \frac{3}{4} + \frac{9}{20} = \frac{6}{5}
B = \sum_{n=1}^{2} \prod_{k=1}^{n} \left(1-\frac{k}{3}\right) = \frac{2}{3} + \frac{2}{9} = \frac{8}{9}
S_3 = A - B = \frac{6}{5} - \frac{8}{9} = \frac{54 - 40}{45} = \frac{14}{45}

